{"version": 2, "width": 80, "height": 24, "timestamp": 1784684532, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "xterm-256color"}}
[0.004688, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m# BEAT 1 — meet alice. On the SOURCE she is a member of 'in-scope-role', and the\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# ACL authorizes that role to write to 'pageviews'. Acting as alice:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.005013, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[31m$\u001b[0m\u001b[1m echo 'page-view-1' | alice_src topic produce pageviews\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.045183, "o", "Produced to partition 0 at offset 0 with timestamp 1784684540636.\r\n"]
[8.047302, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m# Works. The SHADOW already has that ACL — mirrored by ACL sync — but NO\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# role behind it: role sync is NOT configured (filter section, bottom of\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# the SHADOW window). The exact same action against the SHADOW:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[31m$\u001b[0m\u001b[1m echo 'page-view-2' | alice_dst topic produce pageviews\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.070212, "o", "unable to produce record: TOPIC_AUTHORIZATION_FAILED: Not authorized to access topics: [Topic authorization failed.]\r\n"]
[16.071069, "o", "\u001b[2m(check ok: denied as expected)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.071113, "o", "\r\n"]
[16.071129, "o", "\u001b[2m# Denied. The mirrored ACL grants to a role that doesn't exist here —\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.071142, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m# the inert state from slide 2. This is what failover would look like.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.094884, "o", "\u001b[2m(check ok: role staged on source)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.123742, "o", "\u001b[2m(check ok: alice is the staged member)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.148839, "o", "\u001b[2m(check ok: bob not a member yet)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.174048, "o", "\u001b[2m(check ok: role absent on shadow)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.194163, "o", "\u001b[2m(check ok: ACL present on source)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.216596, "o", "\u001b[2m(check ok: ACL mirrored to shadow)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.24425, "o", "\u001b[2m(check ok: role sync not configured yet)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.244277, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m# BEAT 2 — role sync is opt-in. This is the config we're adding to the link:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[31m$\u001b[0m\u001b[1m cat lib/role-sync-options.yaml\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[24.246718, "o", "role_sync_options:\r\n  interval: 5s\r\n  role_name_filters:\r\n    - pattern_type: PREFIX\r\n      filter_type: INCLUDE\r\n      name: in-scope\r\n"]
[24.24698, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m# (rpk shadow update is editor-based; EDITOR here is a script that\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# splices that block into the link config — one command on stage.)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[31m$\u001b[0m\u001b[1m EDITOR=lib/editor-add-role-sync.sh dst_rpk shadow update demo-link\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[32.298431, "o", "Successfully updated shadow link \"demo-link\".\r\n"]
[33.35333, "o", "\u001b[2m(converged in 1s)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[33.353359, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m# ...the PRE-EXISTING role converged, alice's membership included,\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# without anyone touching the role. Same alice action on the SHADOW:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[31m$\u001b[0m\u001b[1m echo 'page-view-3' | alice_dst topic produce pageviews\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[41.396689, "o", "Produced to partition 0 at offset 0 with timestamp 1784684573988.\r\n"]
[41.39911, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m# Authorized. The mirrored ACL finally has a role behind it — exactly\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# what a failover needs. And it keeps flowing: membership changes on\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# the source sync too.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[31m$\u001b[0m\u001b[1m src_rpk security role assign in-scope-role --principal User:bob\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[49.451207, "o", "Successfully assigned role \"in-scope-role\" to\r\nNAME  PRINCIPAL-TYPE\r\nbob   User\r\n"]
[53.615467, "o", "\u001b[2m(converged in 4s)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[53.615738, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m# ...bob appears in BOTH membership sections. One more look at the\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# message sections: they did\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# NOT converge. Role sync moved authorization, not data — topic\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[53.615762, "o", "\u001b[2m# shadowing is its own opt-in, and it's off ('No topics are being\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# shadowed', SHADOW window).\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# BEAT 3 — the gotcha: edit an IN-SCOPE role ON THE SHADOW; the source wins\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[31m$\u001b[0m\u001b[1m dst_rpk security role assign in-scope-role --principal User:charlie\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[61.655205, "o", "Successfully assigned role \"in-scope-role\" to\r\nNAME     PRINCIPAL-TYPE\r\ncharlie  User\r\n"]
[62.716355, "o", "\u001b[2m(converged in 1s)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# ...charlie stripped. Now the contrast: create an OUT-OF-SCOPE role on\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# the shadow — no in-scope prefix, so sync never reads, changes, or\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# deletes it. It just stays.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[31m$\u001b[0m\u001b[1m dst_rpk security role create out-scope-dst-role\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[70.755947, "o", "Successfully created role \"out-scope-dst-role\"\r\n\r\nACLs can now be added to this role using\r\n  rpk security acl create --allow-role \"RedpandaRole:out-scope-dst-role\" [acl-flags]\r\n\r\nCheck 'rpk security acl create --help' for more information about how to create \r\nan ACL. \r\n"]
[70.782763, "o", "\u001b[2m(check ok: out-of-scope shadow role present)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[70.782863, "o", "\r\n"]
[70.782917, "o", "\u001b[2m# BEAT 4 — full mirror IN SCOPE: delete on the source; 'in-scope-role' vanishes\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# from the shadow — while 'out-scope-dst-role' is never touched.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[31m$\u001b[0m\u001b[1m src_rpk security role delete in-scope-role --no-confirm\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[78.810549, "o", "PERMISSIONS\r\n===========\r\nPRINCIPAL                   HOST  RESOURCE-TYPE  RESOURCE-NAME  RESOURCE-PATTERN-TYPE  OPERATION  PERMISSION  ERROR\r\nRedpandaRole:in-scope-role  *     TOPIC          pageviews      LITERAL                WRITE      ALLOW\r\n\r\nPRINCIPALS (2)\r\n==============\r\nNAME   TYPE\r\nalice  User\r\nbob    User\r\n"]
[78.82784, "o", "Successfully deleted role \"in-scope-role\"\r\n"]
[82.973689, "o", "\u001b[2m(converged in 4s)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[82.99938, "o", "\u001b[2m(check ok: out-of-scope shadow role survived)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# done — opt-in; in scope, a full mirror that makes authorization real\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m# at failover; out of scope, invisible.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
